  "body": "The following resolves correctly - `new URL('.\\\\asdf', 'https://some/url').href === 'https://some/asdf'`.\r\n\r\nBut according to the spec,\r\n\r\n```js\r\nimport '.\\\\asdf.js'\r\n```\r\n\r\nwill throw an error as it is detected as a bare module specifier in the module script resolver.\r\n\r\nI'm wondering if perhaps this constraint should be relaxed to include `\\\\` as well?",
